WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.292 --> 00:00:02.586
Bob:
This is the Land of Luck.

00:00:02.586 --> 00:00:05.255
It’s so wonderful to think
outside of what we know. 

00:00:05.255 --> 00:00:07.925
And to entertain the thoughts
that there is more

00:00:07.925 --> 00:00:11.303
Eva:
and that there is bigger and
that there is deeper and there is wider.

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:14.139
We don’t live in a world without
storytelling.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.017
Whoopi:
And that’s the thing that keeps
the world going.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:21.688
Films can expand what’s
possible and expand the
imagination and

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:24.107
can open peoples hearts and
minds.

00:00:24.107 --> 00:00:27.653
Luck, it’s incredibly uplifting
and it’s incredibly positive.

00:00:27.653 --> 00:00:29.446
Is he thoughtful or what?

00:00:29.446 --> 00:00:31.907
And the concept just seemed
utterly bananas.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:38.288
Luck is all about Sam, the
unluckiest girl in the world.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:40.666
-Oh!
-Uhh..

00:00:40.916 --> 00:00:42.251
Sorry to bother you.

00:00:42.251 --> 00:00:46.046
Ouch! How did it get on your..

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:49.383
Peggy:
Who journeys to the never before
seen Land of Luck 

00:00:49.383 --> 00:00:51.677
Peggy:
and discovers really what good
luck is all about.

00:00:51.677 --> 00:00:52.386
Sam:
Oww!

00:00:52.386 --> 00:00:53.637
Eva
The Land of Luck is

00:00:53.637 --> 00:00:59.101
in charge of creating and
randomly distributing luck both
good and bad to the human world.

00:00:59.101 --> 00:01:02.688
The luck you create today could
change a life tomorrow.

00:01:02.688 --> 00:01:05.148
It’s magical. It’s the land of
luck,

00:01:05.148 --> 00:01:06.066
Whoopi:
but it's organized.

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.026
Now drop your pennies and move
along.

00:01:08.026 --> 00:01:10.070
Say captain, do you like
jokes?

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.863
Only the funny ones Bob.

00:01:11.863 --> 00:01:12.739
(Laughing)
Right.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:15.367
Bob is this very mischievous

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:17.619
not entirely professional
worker in the Land of Luck. 

00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:19.871
Hey Bob, everything ok? 

00:01:19.871 --> 00:01:23.375
Aye just uh, stretching my legs.

00:01:23.375 --> 00:01:24.167
Okie dokie.

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:27.379
Sam accidentally goes through
the portal with Bob.

00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:28.588
Aww!

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:30.716
What kind of a crazy talking cat
are you?

00:01:30.716 --> 00:01:32.884
A lucky Scottish one obviously.

00:01:32.884 --> 00:01:34.469
Several things are very
critical.

00:01:34.469 --> 00:01:39.349
Jane:
One is to keep good luck and bad
luck separated.

00:01:39.349 --> 00:01:44.938
The tiniest amount of bad luck
can shut down our entire
operation.

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:49.359
Another is human beings cannot
set foot in the Land of Luck.

00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:50.694
What could go wrong?

00:01:51.069 --> 00:01:53.947
(Boys &amp; Girls)
Aww!

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:58.368
I love animation as a way of
storytelling because it is so
collaborative.

00:01:58.368 --> 00:02:00.787
Peggy:
And then you get to sort of
create the world.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:03.790
Peggy:
You actually create the soul of
the characters.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:06.001
(Gasp)
Jeff’s a unicorn!?

00:02:06.001 --> 00:02:10.213
(Screaming)
Ah, Oh you surprised my heart to
stop. 

00:02:10.213 --> 00:02:14.134
The very, very first week on the
movie when I was trying, we were
trying

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:16.219
to sort of think about what
should this story be.

00:02:16.219 --> 00:02:18.597
Peggy:
I asked the artists in the art
department

00:02:18.597 --> 00:02:24.436
and all the story artists to
just literally for three days
come up with drawings

00:02:24.436 --> 00:02:26.480
Peggy:
of good luck creatures and bad
luck creatures.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.440
Peggy:
Based on research we had done.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:32.027
on sort of international lucky
icons from all over the world.

00:02:32.027 --> 00:02:36.239
Along with lucky numbers, lucky
colors, we had done a huge
amount of research.

00:02:36.239 --> 00:02:38.450
And that was their first
assignment, just go crazy.

00:02:40.911 --> 00:02:43.997
Luck is actually sort of an
abstract idea right?

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:49.336
Ernie:
So the biggest challenge was
coming up with a world that represented that idea.

00:02:49.336 --> 00:02:54.383
Luck is very universal, but very
different in different cultures.

00:02:54.383 --> 00:02:56.635
So immediately the leprechaun
came to mind.

00:02:56.635 --> 00:02:58.762
Clarisse:
As well as the four leaf
clovers

00:02:58.762 --> 00:02:59.679
Clarisse:
and the pig.

00:03:00.389 --> 00:03:02.974
Ernie:
The Land of Luck it’s a world of
synchronicity.

00:03:02.974 --> 00:03:05.227
Ernie:
It’s just really fun to watch
there’s a choreography to it.

00:03:05.227 --> 00:03:08.146
If it wasn’t a lucky place it
would actually be quite
treacherous.

00:03:08.146 --> 00:03:09.523
Ernie:
And it is for Sam.

00:03:09.523 --> 00:03:10.607
Oww!

00:03:10.607 --> 00:03:11.608
♪♪

00:03:11.608 --> 00:03:14.319
Just how unlucky are you?

00:03:14.319 --> 00:03:16.238
Yeah, super duper.

00:03:16.238 --> 00:03:18.740
Peggy:
This is an animated film but
these actors

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:22.702
invested 500% on what is their
character.

00:03:22.994 --> 00:03:27.082
Sam is wonderfully determined
and she is, I think extremely
optimistic.

00:03:27.082 --> 00:03:29.042
Ok Universe, you think you’re
pretty tough? 

00:03:29.251 --> 00:03:30.752
Eva:
Her luck hinders her.

00:03:32.129 --> 00:03:33.713
Eva:
But nevertheless, she persists.

00:03:34.381 --> 00:03:37.217
Simon:
Eva, just really gets to the
heart of that character.

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.635
Take that universe.

00:03:38.844 --> 00:03:42.139
She’s utterly delightful and you
root for her so much.

00:03:42.139 --> 00:03:45.851
I found an actual lucky penny
and what did I do?

00:03:45.851 --> 00:03:47.102
I flushed it down the toilet!

00:03:47.811 --> 00:03:49.229
You did what!?

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:51.648
You flushed my lucky penny down
the toilet!?

00:03:51.648 --> 00:03:53.150
Simon is a legend.

00:03:53.483 --> 00:03:56.987
Eva:
He is a comedic genius and he
brings so much life to Bob.

00:03:56.987 --> 00:03:59.239
What manner of crazy human are
you?

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.366
Simon:
To play this sort of guide into
that world,

00:04:01.366 --> 00:04:02.492
it just, it felt like a gift.

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:05.620
Eva:
Bob knows the Land of Luck
inside out.

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:07.164
Eva:
He has good ideas.

00:04:07.164 --> 00:04:10.584
Eva
Together they create the perfect
team with determination and execution.

00:04:11.585 --> 00:04:15.172
We lucky ladies of stature ought
to stick together don’t ya
think?

00:04:15.172 --> 00:04:17.382
Jane Fonda as a dragon when they
told me I was like,

00:04:17.382 --> 00:04:20.093
perfect casting, check mark, I
love you.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:23.263
I mean it’s not everyday you get
a chance to voice a dragon...

00:04:23.638 --> 00:04:24.055
Aww!

00:04:24.055 --> 00:04:25.640
Jane:
...named Babe. (chuckle)

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.517
I just thought that was so much
fun.

00:04:27.684 --> 00:04:28.685
(Sirens &amp; tires skidding)

00:04:28.685 --> 00:04:29.936
Bob:
Ah! It’s the captain!

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:32.856
I love animation, so anytime
someone asks me

00:04:32.856 --> 00:04:35.192
Whoopi:
if I want to do an animation
I say yes.

00:04:35.192 --> 00:04:35.984
I love Whoopi,

00:04:35.984 --> 00:04:40.238
she’s a fantastic actor and has
a brilliant comedic sensibility
as well.

00:04:40.906 --> 00:04:41.698
Wasn’t funny.

00:04:41.698 --> 00:04:44.451
You’ve not really seen a black
leprechaun before.

00:04:44.451 --> 00:04:46.661
I haven’t, and I’ve met many.

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:49.706
Simon:
This is one of those kinds of
films where you have to watch it once

00:04:49.706 --> 00:04:52.626
just to take it in and then
you can sort of concentrate
on the story.

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:54.294
Eva:
Sam goes on this wonderful
journey of 

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:58.590
discovering that just because
she’s clumsy or things break or
things don’t work out 

00:04:58.590 --> 00:04:59.424
it doesn’t mean it’s her fault.

00:04:59.841 --> 00:05:00.175
Oww!

00:05:00.175 --> 00:05:04.721
Sam:
Bad luck led me to the luckiest
thing in the world or was it good luck?

00:05:04.721 --> 00:05:06.973
Love is the luckiest thing in
the world.

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:10.560
So I really wanted to tell that
story that everybody can feel
the love 

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.521
your forever family can look
different.

00:05:12.521 --> 00:05:14.439
♪♪

00:05:14.439 --> 00:05:18.235
It’s just a lovely story about
the importance of friendship and
family 

00:05:18.235 --> 00:05:20.320
Simon:
and it’s a rip roaring adventure
as well.

00:05:20.612 --> 00:05:24.074
I like the idea that we’re
changing hearts and minds
through this.

00:05:24.074 --> 00:05:26.201
Jane:
The important message is don't
give up.

00:05:26.201 --> 00:05:27.702
Jane:
Don’t ever give up.

00:05:27.702 --> 00:05:30.247
Because you don’t know what the
future might hold.

00:05:30.997 --> 00:05:34.584
Eva:
This movie brings humanity into
the idea of making mistakes.

00:05:34.584 --> 00:05:36.503
You can’t plan everything to go
well

00:05:36.503 --> 00:05:38.463
Eva:
and when you fall you pick
yourself up again,

00:05:38.463 --> 00:05:39.297
Eva:
that's life.

00:05:39.297 --> 00:05:41.591
♪♪

